cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Sigma-GLYPH: a portable deterministic check engine with size-priced budgets"
abstract: >-
  A content-addressed computation core: send a term by hash with a budget, and any
  machine returns the same result hash — deterministic, integer-only, total, with
  no clock and no network. One budget prices both work and peak memory, so
  re-running a stranger's computation is safe by construction. Determinism,
  totality and the memory bound are mechanised in Lean 4; three independent
  implementations agree on every conformance vector. A wave/coordinate layer sits
  above as a view over identity and never as part of it.
message: "If you use or evaluate this work, please cite it."
